# what links.yml is told not to check, each line a regex and each with
# the measurement that put it here.

# gmplib.org answers a developer machine and times out for a runner.
# From a workstation this answers 200 in about a second, at most:
#   curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code} %{time_total}\n' \
#     https://gmplib.org/manual/Low_002dlevel-Functions
# From the runner, the weekly run 39018754822 (2026-10-17) and the dispatch
# 39298170565 (2026-10-19) each ended with this one [TIMEOUT] in
# SECURITY.md, past the retries and timeout reusable-links.yml gives lychee;
# the 2026-10-11 run, the last before SECURITY.md cited the page, was
# green. The citation stays: it is the GMP manual's list of the functions
# written for side-channel resistance, which SECURITY.md's gmpy2 paragraph
# rests on, and only the check is skipped.
^https://gmplib\.org/manual/Low_002dlevel-Functions$
